data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":1267,"item_id":"msg_0b6d44bd578fa1ca016adb4445f16c8191932642ffe33edc2c","output_index":0,"content_index":0,"text":"{\"inference\":\"R001\",\"packet_sha256\":\"aa6d2d87ccd3462d4aa5b7a25d9a2c1595a3653036998dfd2b71ae1ff55ca2cf\",\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Fresh packet-only mathematical review: the only mathematical task material read was packet.json, together with the declared Yui Audit A, self-containment, and format rules. Inputs are treated as conditional premises; this is not a source-fidelity review or carrier-identity/runtime attestation. The proof route is internally sufficient: S001 supplies the basis and divided-power calculations; S002 obtains matrix units; S003 proves the coordinate module is rank-one free; S004 transfers the basis and actions; and S005–S008 establish irreducibility and close the cases. I find no unsupported implication requiring external mathematical material.\",\"checks\":{\"inputs\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"All cited inputs are the four listed hypotheses. Their parameter conditions and roles are used in the basis, localization, reduction, and module arguments; no unlisted source proposition is invoked.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/0\",\"/inputs/1\",\"/inputs/2\",\"/inputs/3\",\"/inference/inputs\"]},\"argument\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The calculation and module-theoretic steps are given in the prose. In particular, the rank-one step does not assume J free: it computes the Q-dimension, embeds the torsion-free localization, clears denominators, and proves the resulting ideal is principal by the p-adic exponent calculation. The matrix-unit argument handles the endpoint and lambda=0 cases.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"/inference/argument/3/text\",\"/inference/argument/4/text\",\"/inference/argument/5/text\",\"/inference/argument/6/text\",\"/inference/argument/7/text\"]},\"dependency_accounting\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Factual uses are supported by listed H inputs, earlier local facts F001/F002/F003, definitions introduced in scope, or displayed calculations. The calculation-policy sentence is not a substitute for the substantive arguments; no named external theorem is merely applied.\",\"locations\":[\"/logic/calculations\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"/inference/argument/3/text\",\"/inference/argument/5/text\",\"/inference/argument/6/text\",\"/inference/argument/7/text\"]},\"output\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The conclusion is precisely that M tensor_Z K is nonzero and every invariant K-subspace under x,y,h is zero or the whole module. S004 establishes the basis correspondence, and S008 establishes both properties.\",\"locations\":[\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/argument/3/text\",\"/inference/argument/7/text\"]},\"scope\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"W is introduced arbitrarily; L1 is confined to the nonzero branch, and F002/F003 and the chosen witnesses are used only there. The two cases establish the conclusion for arbitrary W; positive dimension establishes nonzeroness.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/locals/13\",\"/inference/locals/18\",\"/inference/locals/19\",\"/inference/argument/4\",\"/inference/argument/5\",\"/inference/argument/6\",\"/inference/argument/7\"]},\"applicability\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"There are no E/M source inputs or source-theorem applications. The H inputs are used at the stated parameter values; reduction uses p prime, characteristic p, and lambda<p.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/inputs\",\"/inference/applications\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/argument/3/text\",\"/inference/argument/4/text\"]},\"statement_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The input/output propositions state the relevant hypotheses and conclusion. The proof spells out the basis, action formulas, coordinate modules, scalar-extension identifications, and invariant-subspace property rather than relying on theorem names or inherited references.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/0/statement\",\"/inputs/1/statement\",\"/inputs/2/statement\",\"/inputs/3/statement\",\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/argument\"]},\"object_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The objects used in the prose have packet declarations as parameters, primitives, input-bound objects, or local definitions/witnesses. Indexed matrix-unit occurrences are instances of the stated matrix-unit definition; witnesses a, w0, and i have local existence bases.\",\"locations\":[\"/parameters\",\"/logic/primitives\",\"/inference/locals\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"/inference/argument/5/text\",\"/inference/argument/6/text\"]},\"dependency_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Reverse inspection finds no ancestor-proof or ambient-H dependency: each substantive step is in this inference text, a listed H, or a previously produced local fact. S003’s principal-ideal conclusion is supported by its explicit valuation argument, not a hidden PID citation.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/inputs\",\"/inference/argument/0\",\"/inference/argument/1\",\"/inference/argument/2\",\"/inference/argument/3\",\"/inference/argument/4\",\"/inference/argument/5\",\"/inference/argument/6\",\"/inference/argument/7\"]},\"packet_replay\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"I reviewed the complete frozen packet in this context with the declared procedure rules and no other mathematical task material. On that boundary, the packet suffices for the conditional proof. This does not authenticate carrier identity, canonical-hash binding, transmission/readback, or runtime isolation beyond the supplied interaction.\",\"locations\":[\"/packet_sha256\",\"/warning\",\"/inference/argument\"]}},\"findings\":[]}","logprobs":[]}

